<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>Comparison of classification accuracy (%) across datasets. Baselines cover diverse categories. <span id="S4.T1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FETA</span> variants are compared under the same evaluation. Best results per dataset are in <span id="S4.T1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bold</span>, and second-best results are <span id="S4.T1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">underlined</span>. <span id="S4.T1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FETA</span> achieves
the highest accuracy, driven by multivariate series decomposition, DTW-aligned exemplars retrieval, channel-level in-context reasoning, and confidence-weighted aggregation.</figcaption>
</figure>
